significantly higher for wo) Tj T* (  men, by about 15%. The total excess mortality for women \(+9378 deaths\) was 75% higher than that for men \(+5351 deaths\).) Tj T* (Excess mortality by place of death) Tj T* (Major excess mortalities were observed for deaths at home \(+5130 deaths\), in retirement homes \(+2574 deaths\) and in public hospitals \(+5996 deaths\). T) Tj T* (  he relative increase in mortality at home \(+74%\) and in retirement homes \(+91%\) was, however, markedly greater than that observed in public hospital) Tj T* (  s \(+45%\) and private clinics \(+22%\). This was observed both globally and by age group \(table 2\).) Tj T* (Table 2.) Tj T* (Excess deaths by place of death, marital status, number of “very hot days” and age - France, August 1st to 20th, 2003.) Tj T* (;) Tj T* (< 55 years) Tj T* (;) Tj T* (55–74 years) Tj T* (;) Tj T* (? 75 years) Tj T* ET
